this is something fans of winter sports  won't be seeing again anytime soon  this year the swiss resort of davos  clusters celebrated 150 years of winter  sports with a nostalgic bobsled and  toboggan race  the first ever time toboggan race was  held right here in 1883.  the race featured dozens of vintage  toboggan sleds dating from 1890 the  1930s and the 1960s  a few other rather unusual creations  also went to the starting line  the participants included amateur  tobogganers and champion bobsledders  like eckahart fossur olympic gold  medalist european and world champion and  world cup winner  back then he raced through winding ice  tunnels  conditions today aren't quite the same  it's so warm right now that this isn't  ice  it's just packed snow  and these bobsleds aren't really suited  for racing on snow  that's no obstacle for the former pro  athlete  but less experienced participants have  to resort to creative tactics  this is how it looked one day earlier  it's a road  race organizer klaus holler and his  colleagues from the international  tobogganing club in davos had to  recreate the old bobsled and toboggan  run in weather that was plus two degrees  celsius  building the curve especially with the  warm temperatures we're having right now  was a real challenge  first we had to prepare all the blocks  of ice and after that we built  everything  tomorrow we'll have to cover the entire  road with snow which will be a lot of  work  800 cubic meters of snow and a year of  preparation 150 years of winter sports  has lots of history behind it  friedrich  and hugo richter from germany were the  first two winter tourists in davos  clusters back in 1865.  in 1879 tobogganing joined the modern  era legend has it that two englishmen  held the first timed race here  local residents turned that into  bobsledding  in 1872 the first curling event took  place  and in 1890 the first ever ski tour was  organized here  that was soon followed by ice hockey  the resort has another highlight for  visitors this natural skating rink  opened in 1880  the largest drink of its kind in europe  it's popular with amateur skaters  and the pros  the long tradition of winter sports is  immortalized in the davos museum which  has many old artifacts in its collection  including toboggans  bobsleds  and vintage skis  it's winter sports that made the small  resort in switzerland famous  though davos has just 15 000 residents  today it's among the world's top winter  destinations  about 360 000 tourists come here each  year  more than twice as many as 50 years ago  i'm from alicante in spain i'm here for  the weekend to ski conditions are very  good and we're enjoying ourselves here  i came from belarus and this is my  second time in davos i'm from moscow  russia and i like davos a lot and i  think it's the best resort in  switzerland  the nostalgic toboggan and bobsled race  has also drawn an international audience  here to enjoy the event that had its  start with winter tourists from britain  it just sort of feels part of the  heritage of the swiss swiss winter  sports and swiss winter tourism which  the english  have done we've been so involved over so  many years  as long as the snow holds out davos  hopes to remain a popular destination  for fans of winter sports
 

